1: before
  WHEN EC-USER-A [ecperform; m1 OF main; 30]
  WHEN COMMON
1: after the raise, resumed
  WHEN OTHER: EC-USER-B
  WHEN COMMON
1: finally
2: after END-PERFORM, EC-USER-A is off again:
3: turned on outside, its USE declarative runs:
  USE for EC-USER-A
4: a fatal condition in a PERFORM:
  WHEN EC-BOUND-SUBSCRIPT, then the run ends
